.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH export 1  "export " 
.SH NAME
export \- Export a snippet as YAML (to stdout or a file)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBexport\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export a snippet as YAML (to stdout or a file)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Write to this file instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Snippet name
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg export ubuntu\-setup \-\-out ubuntu\-setup.yaml
